Build diagnostics_log without //sdk/lib/syslog:client_includes (milestone M9b).

Upstream's own comment: an empty stub in Bazel; in GN an expect_includes() target that
checks that dependent components include syslog/client.shard.cml in their manifest. The
overlay does not vendor //sdk/lib/syslog, so the label is removed; the manifest check is
the driver package's concern (milestone M10).

The added lines are the overlay's (Apache-2.0); the context lines are Fuchsia's
(BSD-2-Clause, LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt). Applied by scripts/regen.py to the rewritten
BUILD.bazel.

--- a/src/lib/diagnostics/log/rust/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/src/lib/diagnostics/log/rust/BUILD.bazel
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
         "//vendor/fuchsia/sdk/fidl/fuchsia.logger:fuchsia.logger_rust",
         # Empty stub in Bazel; an expect_includes() target in GN that checks
         # dependent components for `syslog/client.shard.cml` in their manifest.
-        "//vendor/fuchsia/sdk/lib/syslog:client_includes",
+        # Overlay: removed; the manifest check is milestone M10's (patch 0001).
         "//vendor/fuchsia/sdk/rust/zx",
         "//vendor/fuchsia/src/lib/diagnostics/log/encoding/rust",
         "//vendor/fuchsia/src/lib/fidl/rust/fidl",
